    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">You&#39;re passing the <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">data</font> argument to <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">lm</font> as a string instead of a variable. I.e., on startup, for example,<font face=\"courier new, monospace\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">input$dsname</span> </font>is equal to <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">&quot;Aids2&quot;</font> (a character vector), not  <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Aids2</font> (a data.frame).<div><br></div><div>If you change<span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">  <font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">data </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> input$dsname</span></font><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span></span>to  <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">data = eval(parse(text = input$dsname))</font><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"> , it should work fine.</font></div></div>"
    ],
    [
